Z||000000||72vinman||08-20-2001||09:07 PM||||I was just outside playin' around under the hood and noticed something wierd. The back of the air filter cannister there is a hose that looks like it was once connected to it. When I follow the hose acroos the back of the engine bay it ends right in the middle with a steele connector. Should this be conected to something, I don't see any other hose that might of come loose. Any thoughts. Thanks<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Stock Black 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by 72vinman (edited 08-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||08-20-2001||09:18 PM||||That hose was disconnected as part of a recall.  Its only purpose in life now is to sit there and cause confusion!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||72vinman||08-20-2001||09:25 PM||||It looks like the hole where it used to be connected is pluged up. Should I unplug it?<P>------------------<BR>72vinman@home.com<BR>Stock Black 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||08-20-2001||09:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 72vinman:<BR><B>It looks like the hole where it used to be connected is pluged up. Should I unplug it?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>This has come up a couple of times in the last few mos. I have a 4cyl so I'm not real familar with it but if my memory is not faulty(fat chance) The answer is to leave it plugged. I think Galen answered the last inquiry, Try him or a search in tech .<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||08-20-2001||09:47 PM||||Leave the hole in the air cleaner housing plugged up.  It makes no difference if the hose that runs along the firewall is plugged or left open.  It used to be part of the crankcase ventilation system, but it got re-plumbed during a recall.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
